module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.instrument_refusal_before_subject_reads_as_a_subject_verdict

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data instrument_refusal_before_subject_reads_as_a_subject_verdict: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "instrument_refusal_before_subject_reads_as_a_subject_verdict" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**an instrument's refusal before reaching its subject collapses into the same Bool as a verdict about the subject** (INVALID STATE: the instrument's report is a Bool, or a success/exit pair, and a refusal at an admission the run had to pass on the way in -- here the compiler's workspace-root admission of the staged tree -- becomes the same value a real finding about the subject would. THE GENUINELY FALSE-GREEN SHAPE IS THE EXPECT-FAILURE ARM: an assertion that 'the compile must fail' is SATISFIED by the pre-subject refusal whatever the subject is, so it passes while testing nothing. The expect-success arms fail instead, and their failure reads as a finding about the subject when the subject was never reached. HARM: both directions misattribute -- a red wall that holds nothing, and a red that sends a reader debugging a subject nobody compiled.)",

    "THE DISTINGUISHING FACT: the refusal cause is the workspace-root admission of a /tmp stage, never the subject. Four instruments stage their subject with a bare shell.Mktemp.Dir, which lands outside the checkout, and the compiler refuses such a stage before resolving anything -- 'primary source root is outside the workspace root' on a whole-root argv, 'entry file is outside the workspace root' on an --entry argv. Staged under the workspace, the same compiles run to their subject: the staged std.logic compile exits 0 with one file emitted, and the cross-tree import green exits 0 with zero blocking errors. The subject was never the cause.",

    "THE RECEIPTS, by instrument name. EXECUTED ON MAIN by proud-tern-390 at 653ac639: test.claim.dag_compile_clean_seam_witness cross_shard_seam_preservation_holds_on_live_tree, test.claim.dag_compile_clean_shard_a_witness compile_clean_shard_a_exemplar_compile_green, and test.claim.long.dag_compile_clean_perturb_corpus perturb_cross_tree_import_corpus_green_holds and perturb_dag_shell_primary_corpus_green_holds all FAIL, each with the exact root-admission line 'primary source root is outside the workspace root' -- so none of the four is a passing report; each is an assertion that has never been evaluated against its subject. The same four were measured false in the per-instrument table on gunbc#11265 (session nimble-badger-98, session container), with the pre-change binary refusing the same /tmp stage at root-admission. THE DISCRIMINATING CONTROL BESIDE THEM: test.claim.dag_compile_clean_perturb_receipts perturb_fixture_green_holds and its two expect-failure reds return true in that session, because tools.dag_compile_clean_transport dcc_fixture_perturb_compile_expecting stages under target/ inside the workspace -- same transport, same compile shape, one variable, opposite outcomes.",

    "WHY THE REDS ARE THE DANGEROUS HALF, AND NOT THE GREENS. An expect-failure arm over a stage the compiler refuses PASSES whatever the subject is: the refusal satisfies 'the compile must fail'. The perturb reds in this population happen to stage inside the workspace and so do reach their subject; any red that staged in /tmp would read as a held wall while testing nothing. The same collapse makes a green unreachable and a red vacuous, so neither direction of the report can be trusted without knowing which admission refused.",

    "BOUNDARY AGAINST [[an_unreached_measurement_renders_as_a_failed_one]], THE NEAREST ROW, which shares the shape 'never reached its subject, reported like a verdict' and differs in carrier, rung and direction. That row's carrier is a REQUIRED LANE'S RED at the merge surface, and the distinction already exists in a typed field: the adjudication standing is present in the log, so the class sits at rung 1 and its repair is to lift the standing onto the deciding surface. It fails toward WASTE -- nothing is admitted, a red is misattributed. This row's carrier is an INSTRUMENT'S OWN REPORT, a Bool or an exit status returned to a witness, and there is no standing field anywhere to lift: the refusal and the subject verdict are the same value at birth, which is why it is found below the ladder. And it fails OPEN as well as toward waste, because an expect-failure arm turns the pre-subject refusal into a PASS. Repairing that row -- deriving the lane conclusion from its standing -- changes nothing here, since these instruments never produce a standing to derive from.",

    "BOUNDARY AGAINST [[witness_that_fails_to_compile_is_absent_rather_than_red]]: there the WITNESS FILE does not compile, so none of its assertions execute and the claim is absent. Here every witness named compiles and executes; its assertion runs and returns a value. What refuses is the compile the INSTRUMENT drives inside the run, at an admission its subject never reaches, so the witness is present, executing, and wrong about what it measured. Compiling every claim file, that row's trigger, catches none of these four.",

    "BOUNDARY AGAINST THE NEVER-EXECUTED INSTRUMENT, WHICH IS A DIFFERENT CLASS AND IS NOT FOLDED IN HERE: an instrument that is discovered and counted but never executes on the acceptance path at all is read as coverage because it is counted, not because its report collapses a refusal. That class is already recorded for this same compile-clean family as the NO-ROUTE record in gunbc.rung_drop emit_stage_blocking, where these witnesses are refused at the hermetic boundary, discovered and counted and answering nothing. This row owns the collapse inside an executed report; that record owns the counted instrument that never runs. Repairing either leaves the other untouched: a typed RefusedBeforeSubject arm changes nothing for a witness that never executes, and routing a witness onto the floor changes nothing about what its Bool conflates.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: BELOW THE LADDER -- silent wrongness, not mitigation, and located at the EXPECT-FAILURE arms: an assertion that passes on a refusal before its subject is a fabricated plausible output about the compiler, and nothing typed, located or counted distinguished it from a real refusal of the subject. CEILING: 3, structurally guaranteed. REASON: a report coproduct carrying the refusal as its own arm -- RefusedBeforeSubject { admission, cause } beside SubjectVerdict { ... } -- has no constructor that satisfies 'the subject must fail' or 'the subject must pass' for a run that never reached its subject, so a consumer matching on the report cannot mint either verdict from a refusal. It is not 4 because the instrument remains free to construct a SubjectVerdict wrongly; what the coproduct removes is the collapse, not every lie.",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, STATED AS THE CAPABILITY: an instrument report carries refusal-before-subject as its own typed arm, the run's exit status is classified into that arm or into a subject verdict, and the instrument stages its subject under the workspace root -- the capability gunbc#11284 lands for the compile-clean family -- such that THE SUBJECT IS REACHED and every consumer that cites the instrument matches on the arm rather than on a Bool. The trigger fires on the subject being reached and classified; it does NOT fire on the report passing, because a report that passes is exactly what an expect-failure arm already did while measuring nothing, and a red that was already present would otherwise retire this row. SUFFICIENT FOR: every instrument whose run passes an admission before its subject, not only these four.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
